          "min_rill": "0.4.0",
          "url": "https://github.com/m00zu/rill-plugins/releases/download/rill.plot-v0.3.1/rill.plot-0.3.1.rillp",
          "sha256": "ed8364794373792b49eb9e81d401ee8f07f2ac7f85e0a02145c11faa0b63f245",
          "size": 5156045,
          "released": "2026-10-08",
          "notes": "rill.plot 0.3.1 (a fix on the 0.3 line; D113, D120)\n\n- Compose figure: double-click an SVG panel in Focus to touch it up. Hide elements (matplotlib's stray white boxes, for example), change fill and stroke colour, stroke width and opacity, edit real text (words, size, bold, italic), and move elements by dragging or with the arrow keys. A breadcrumb and an element list reach groups and hidden elements.\n- Touch-ups are stored in the panel and follow elements by their SVG id, so re-exporting the SVG from Inkscape keeps them; an edit whose element is gone is listed as no longer matching. The SVG file itself is never changed.\n- An SVG panel's Crop is now a button in the panel tools; image panels keep double-click crop.\n- Saved workflows pick this up on their next run; nothing they already produce changes.",
          "core_hosted": true,
          "requires_plugins": {
            "rill.statistic": ">=1.0,<2"
          },
